gy also allows for sterile and  disposable cartridges  it is safe no aerosols or sample  carryover  the wolf and the wolf viewer software  simple and intuitive  there's a small footprint for both the  wolf and the wolf g2 and can fit easily  in biosafety hoods  and it's affordable  so not only are the wolf and the wolf g2  part of nanaselek's technology but it's  an entire solution for cell sorting  along with the wolf we have the wolf  viewer software and a computer that also  comes with the wolf  there are microfluidic cartridges that  are provided when the wolf is purchased  as well as for individual experiments  and the n1 single cell dispenser  can be included with the wolf for  customers that are doing single cell  experiments  a key innovation for nanoselect and  really where nano's lights all started  is the microfluidic cartridge so we have  two types of cartridges  a bulk sorting cartridge and a single  cell dispensing cartridge which goes on  the single cell the n1 single cell  dispenser  this middle video shows the cell sorting  junction and this is a video of beads  that are flowing through into the  central channel but as they are  triggered by the  by the laser  and the pzt or piezoelectric actuator  they're sorted into that left channel  the pzt  system is actually shown in the cartoon  on the right  and you can see that a positive or  negative charge  allows for cells or any particle to be  sorted into um the a or b  uh channels  so low pressure sorting is important  because conventional cell sorters like  cuvette or jet and air sorters  exert 20 to 70 square inches per pound  of pressure on your cells  which as they exit the nozzle result in  decompression shock  our wolf however emits only  two units of pressure on cells so  there's no decompression shock once they  exit out of the cartridge system  your cells end up being much happier and  healthier and functional for downstream  assays  the closed system is also important for  a couple other rea